//// 1.0.10-beta `00 · 04-js` D9 — a `//` comment inside a braced block.
//// Measured by rakun's front 05.
////
//// A comment written in the source reaches codegen as an EXPRESSION, and
//// commonJS writes some blocks on ONE line (`Block.Layout.spaced`). A `// …`
//// runs to the end of the physical line, so the comment ate the statements
//// after it, the block's own `}` and the `})();` that closed the IIFE — the
//// module was left unterminated and node answered `SyntaxError: Unexpected end
//// of input` at exit 1, where erlang printed `3`. The emitter now spells a line
//// comment `/* … */` wherever the rest of the line still has to survive.

pub fn main() {
    var i = 0;
    if (i == 0) {
        // a comment inside the braced block
        i = 1;
    };
    while (i < 3) {
        // and one inside a condition loop's body
        i = i + 1;
    };
    @print(i);
}
